  "description": "AGGREGATION ... EMPTY reports every bucket in the query window that lies within the series' own extent \u2014 including a bucket past the last in-window sample (data continues beyond the window), one before the first (data precedes it), and a window that is wholly a gap between two samples. RedisTimeSeries 8.10 reports all three; we dropped them, anchoring the fill to the samples the query happened to see (fuzzer finding 2026-08-01). Also pins the `last` fill's seed: a gap bucket inherits the last sample before *the bucket's start*, so a sample inside the first filled bucket but before the window start does not seed it. A retention window makes the same lookup subtle: the retention floor is not a sample timestamp, so a series whose data all postdates it has nothing before the window. And LATEST: the open bucket it chains in can land in a window that lies past everything the destination stores, which is a bucket of its own rather than a reason to fill back toward data ending before the window.",
